[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is a Buffer Overflow. This occurs because the code calculates the `remaining` space in the buffer `buf` by subtracting a fixed offset (14) from `BUF_SIZE`. It then reads data from the file into `buf + 14`. If the file content is larger than `remaining`, the `read` operation will write beyond the allocated bounds of `buf`, overwriting adjacent memory. This overflow can corrupt data or lead to arbitrary code execution.

